["technique_id","T1482"],["technique_ref","attack-pattern--767dbf9e-df3f-45cb-8998-4903ab5f80c0"],["description","To expand the actor’s knowledge of the target’s Active Directory configuration, the graph uses PowerShell to gather information on domain trust relationships that would allow an actor to access additional resources with credentials from their current domain. Additionally, BloodHound is executed to reveal hidden relationships within the targeted Active Directory environment."],["confidence",null],["execution_start",null],["execution_end",null]]},{"id":"77c96daa-d771-4be8-8539-d9b034323755","x":2421,"y":120,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__line_horizontal_elbow","children":["2acd9411-e7fb-4bdf-a00c-b322ee515518","d6b09de0-abdf-4831-bf4f-18bd57957098","066a9e9a-11af-400e-ae68-e49b53562cc9"],"properties":[]},{"id":"255bb67c-3e5f-4e1b-aa82-1a44aa6ae047","x":2350,"y":790,"attrs":256,"template":"action","children":["35aee445-fa93-4b7f-8cec-6c45e2239ac8","547c9c02-e3cb-4003-a0b6-87271b32bc1e","5d893a23-1e05-42c2-bdf4-423904bb4b82","65ecea20-b238-480d-be13-ce366e4d9004","c66b2539-3606-43ab-bba0-bd33417923e6","b11c2c63-93c9-48dc-b03a-3830618ce5fc","c169d56a-7251-4088-9adf-e6915e5b2a7b","f1c8dda1-9974-47b3-810c-d16d9e255e9d","2a28615e-93e7-44d5-89df-99ab7b5b8379","72e386e1-1119-4f63-acf7-a61b6a776771","dd1f4ae8-a857-4ab1-9b79-7b122ed9c980","5fc6f8d0-3fd8-43f2-906a-bd5316fd1976"],"properties":[["name","Exploitation of Remote Services"],["tactic_id","TA0008"],["tactic_ref","x-mitre-tactic--7141578b-e50b-4dcc-bfa4-08a8dd689e9e"],["technique_id","T1210"],["technique_ref","attack-pattern--9db0cf3a-a3c9-4012-8268-123b9db6fd82"],["description","Gaining access to the domain controller is one of the primary goals of Russian threat groups. The attack graph attempts to exploit the Zerologon vulnerability to gain domain administrator privileges."],["confidence",null],["execution_start",null],["execution_end",null]]},{"id":"36af2208-0c14-485a-b86c-2fd95b7bf4d9","x":2505,"y":475,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__line_vertical_elbow","children":["3360126d-bb0d-4285-8d9e-3482c87a6ebc","21ea41b9-b0d1-481c-adef-51e19b211bdf","6e7fd929-2c59-429c-be3b-1a2d9d2863df"],"properties":[]},{"id":"4d758193-8e4a-44de-a417-154ffcece5fa","x":1780,"y":790,"attrs":256,"template":"action","children":["8fbe9100-6333-4303-aa69-f2cc9f7f186b","eebd87aa-7643-4999-b517-363d7e7bb1b1","d33b3de6-c4e6-4b7b-a856-60e474e90621","36c5345e-c478-48e4-afdd-b7be3701c509","9dca3953-a467-449f-8419-5e0f6a4c19b2","36563d35-dc60-4252-9c5a-3c091e6b3b85","db9508ae-b155-4caf-9ce0-ec93a5387dcf","448f7647-4254-4ca2-9485-e45b0913d898","c1bab5d8-6b94-4350-a0fc-f1eca20f29bf","718e707d-bc6b-4643-bed0-503c77d4598b","f2b30373-3d28-4dc7-bf42-aede4285ad7f","ee645987-f750-4cff-8745-8dafe879337c"],"properties":[["name","Steal or Forge Kerberos Tickets: Kerberoasting"],["tactic_id","TA0006"],["tactic_ref","x-mitre-tactic--2558fd61-8c75-4730-94c4-11926db2a263"],["technique_id","T1558.003"],["technique_ref","attack-pattern--f2877f7f-9a4c-4251-879f-1224e3006bee"],["description","The threat actors utilize Kerberoasting attacks to increase their permissions by discovering Service Principal Names (SPNs) assigned to user accounts and requesting their Ticket Granting Service (TGS) tickets that allow for login access to privileged assets. For accurate results this scenario requires either existing credentials pre-configured in the assessment or an asset that already has cached Kerberos credentials, like a system that has recently authenticated a user against a domain controller."],["confidence",null],["execution_start",null],["execution_end",null]]},{"id":"57ee24d6-95ac-4f0d-80d7-4a89b6d1f51b","x":2068,"y":790,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__line_horizontal_elbow","children":["fef79115-4b3d-4c8f-b99c-d4fe12d4915b","2839ed1e-6799-4a2f-9fbc-34f983ec7cb2","2f3c6cde-3823-48b5-b7dd-651aff70c72e"],"properties":[]},{"id":"d67bf336-e0b3-4626-bd6f-13a9d2b05acc","x":1170,"y":790,"attrs":256,"template":"action","children":["1b8eb9b5-ec0a-4c8f-bd41-74a63d661cf1","147513ff-c806-4252-9bcf-93c479cbd6d7","fef07baa-031b-4e18-9e48-b876f2ab5223","6bf64cf1-15f2-4ffa-aafb-8a528e423571","f443427e-cf60-4a44-b8a5-18a3da6e2ef0","587e4c8e-7221-4cf9-8455-f8f532fe60f2","3012bbb7-9e0c-41b1-b953-0cf393c646cb","cb6a5445-38f5-4e26-914b-88b9e842d02f","dab830a6-d51a-478d-9139-08ebf07f0ab2","d15eb7b8-6c33-4bb6-813f-ead0c0cf1063","ea9eddcb-8fc3-4b3c-9a30-acca9f7411e0","10ada82e-9102-4f7a-adfa-a9a78052e202"],"properties":[["name","OS Credential Dumping: NTDS"],["tactic_id","TA0006"],["tactic_ref","x-mitre-tactic--2558fd61-8c75-4730-94c4-11926db2a263"],["technique_id","T1003.003"],["technique_ref","attack-pattern--edf91964-b26e-4b4a-9600-ccacd7d7df24"],["description","One of the many end goals of the threat actor is to obtain a copy of the Active Directory database so that it may be attacked offline. Russian actors have been observed dumping the NTDS.dit database from a domain controller once administrative access has been achieved. This scenario needs to be executed on a Domain Controller asset."],["confidence",null],["execution_start",null],["execution_end",null]]},{"id":"4ad3b67b-cc70-4f36-aec4-87012577bd4d","x":1475,"y":790,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__line_horizontal_elbow","children":["5f101de1-5297-4ca7-bd6c-bbb7f9115fa0","cf4b36a0-95bc-4cbc-aa83-bab4bb77d95f","d93200e4-a673-4609-867e-6bb736abdca7"],"properties":[]},{"id":"1988ec00-ab5e-493a-88e9-64ffa00e25dd","x":2,"y":-232,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__anchor","children":[],"properties":[],"angle":1},{"id":"98517890-988a-4711-abc1-e2c8ed7c5bd5","x":90,"y":-232,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__anchor","children":[],"properties":[],"angle":1},{"id":"d736a020-54d4-4297-8a78-fcb4a39257e6","x":178,"y":-232,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__anchor","children":[],"properties":[],"angle":1},{"id":"8c0d779e-1509-4235-b75e-7071b062f6c3","x":266,"y":-146,"attrs":0,"template":"@__builtin__anchor","children":[],"properties":[],"angle":0},{"id":"